Generic web component previews — Phase 1
Validation and handoff, 2026-10-11

Implemented
- Select a TypeScript source in Repositories. The WebComponent contributor discovers native and framework web components, their registration and public property schemas.
- Visual renders the component with its own defaults. The regular node editor adjusts supported scalar properties; Preview retains those trial values. Code retains guarded source editing and saving.
- Components need no uiDefinition, editor metadata, catalog entry or component-specific adapter. The superseded composition catalog/model/shell was removed.
- Render and compilation errors replace the Visual/Preview content while the tabs remain usable. Preview starts at minimum content size and can zoom out to fit.
- Preview documents require authentication and run in a separate sandbox. Real service requests, parent access and storage are unavailable.
- Sample-data setup and service substitutes remain in Phase 2. Phase 2 has not been developed.

